torille licensing
=================

torille is multi-licensed by component. The license is chosen per directory,
not per file, unless a file says otherwise.

Engine, bindings, browser code and examples
-------------------------------------------

Everything outside `tools/` and `data/` is available under either of:

  * the MIT License, in `LICENSE-MIT`; or
  * the Apache License, Version 2.0, in `LICENSE-APACHE`;

at your option. This covers `src/`, `tests/`, `benches/`, `bindings/`,
`wrapper/`, `torille-wasm/`, `torille-wasm-leptos/`, `demo-server/`,
`torille-firefox/`, `torille-chromium/`, `docs/`, `rules/`, and the repository
documentation.

SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT OR Apache-2.0

Tools
-----

The development and verification tooling in `tools/` is licensed like the
engine, except for the files tied to Omorfi or Voikko. Those oracle bridge and
harness files are licensed under the GNU General Public License, version 3 or
later (GPL-3.0-or-later), because Omorfi is GPLv3 and libvoikko is
GPLv2-or-later. The full text is in `tools/LICENSE-GPL-3.0`, and
`tools/README.md` lists the exact files. Each GPL file carries an SPDX header.

SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-3.0-or-later (Omorfi/Voikko harness files only)

Data
----

Files under `data/` are not part of the source code and are not licensed by
this file. They are Kotus data publications with their own terms; see
`data/LICENSE` and `NOTICE`. Nothing in `LICENSE-MIT`, `LICENSE-APACHE`, or
`tools/LICENSE-GPL-3.0` changes those terms.
